DOS-PORT (patch 0109, Phase 10 W22-WB-E DOS 8.3 fix). Renames the
ORGMID-transcribed-MIDI directory from "midi-orgmid" (11 chars,
violates DOS 8.3 directory name limit) to "orgmid" (6 chars, clean).
Three string updates in SoundManager.cpp + docs/BOOT.md to match the
on-disk rename + scripts/build-cs-midi-orgmid.py update (team-lead
performed the on-disk move + script edit 2026-05-07).

Background — caught by additional DOSBox-X smoke 2026-05-07:

After slot 0107 shipped, my original smoke was inconclusive because
data/midi-orgmid/ was empty on my side at the time (got ENOENT
"file not found" which I attributed to graceful-missing-file path).
Per team-lead's surface "data/midi-orgmid/ IS in tree, run the
smoke against it" I re-ran with the dir actually populated and got:

  [error] MidiScheduler::load: cannot open 'data/midi-orgmid/curly.mid':
          errno 22

errno 22 = EINVAL, NOT ENOENT. The file existed on disk; the path
itself was rejected. Root cause: tools/dosbox-x-fast.conf has
`lfn = false` (explicitly mirrors real-HW MS-DOS 6.22 — Phase 8
LFN-Option-B precedent); DOS rejects directory paths containing a
component of >8 chars with EINVAL. data/midi/ (4 chars) works;
data/midi-orgmid/ (11 chars) doesn't.

Per `dos_filename_8_3.md` memory + `dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_-
io.md`: this is one of the few classes of behavior where DOSBox-X
IS a faithful proxy for real-HW (lfn=false matches). Bug would have
hit g2k operator iter as well; better to fix here.

Fix:

  src/sound/SoundManager.cpp:
    _midi_source_dir = "midi-orgmid"  →  _midi_source_dir = "orgmid"
    LOG_INFO banner: "data/midi-orgmid/<name>.mid" → "data/orgmid/<name>.mid"

  docs/BOOT.md slot-0107 entry: data/midi-orgmid/ → data/orgmid/
    Plus added 1-sentence note documenting the DOS 8.3 rename rationale
    so future readers see why the dir name shortened during slot 0109.

Out of scope (already done by team-lead):
  - mv data/midi-orgmid/ data/orgmid/ (41 files, 628KB)
  - scripts/build-cs-midi-orgmid.py default --out-subdir update

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast):

  Pre-fix smoke (slot 0108 binary, with new orgmid dir present):
    Loaded path: data/midi-orgmid/curly.mid
    Result: errno 22 EINVAL → graceful LOG_WARN → music silent

  Post-fix smoke (this slot's binary, with new orgmid dir present):
    Loaded path: data/orgmid/curly.mid
    Result: parsed 7931 events at 24 PPQ → midi-stub on_song_start
    Track change to access.mid: parsed 344 events → on_song_start
    67 flips, no crashes, no errno 22 anywhere in DEBUG.LOG.

  midi-stub on_song_start/stop fired correctly per Stage 2 stub
  validation pattern. Parser handled both songs through track
  changes. ORGMID-transcribed files have 24 PPQ (vs WiiWare's
  480 PPQ) — different SMF division, both supported by the
  MidiScheduler PPQ-based timing.

  Strings-grep confirms binary has NO "midi-orgmid" literal
  (clean) AND HAS "data/orgmid/" literals.

Quality gates per team-lead's dispatch:
  1. ✓ Three string changes applied (SoundManager + BOOT.md)
  2. ✓ DOSBox-X smoke loads data/orgmid/curly.mid cleanly (7931
     events parsed; no errno 22)
  3. ✓ midi-stub + AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE=orgmid path end-to-end works
  4. ✓ Patch applies cleanly on top of slot 0108
  5. ✓ strings-grep confirms no "midi-orgmid" residue + new
     "data/orgmid/" present

Real-HW iter (W22-WB-E PLAY5) will exercise the full path against
g2k Vibra16S OPL3 with operator listening to A/B-compare the
literal-ORGMID transcription vs WiiWare arrangement. The DOS 8.3
fix unblocks that comparison.

Memory note candidates (deferred to user-call):
  - dos_filename_8_3.md addendum: errno 22 EINVAL discriminator
    vs ENOENT for "long dir name vs missing file" debugging
  - dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md addendum: DOS 8.3 file
    system rules ARE faithfully reproduced when lfn=false; one
    of the few classes of behavior where DOSBox-X = real-HW
